From e7d3db18baf785ad9aec5c4771f2c8b51e58af42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:46:54 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] rocket RK3576: B is per channel in the vendor, use
 zero_points[oc]

Decoded from the runtime capture. sv_rgu's B column holds 26 distinct values
across 32 channels, ranging -25 to 23 with a mean of 0.16, and correlates with
nothing tested: not the bias, the weight sum, A, C or the scale. A tight spread
centred on zero is what 0x80 - wt_zp[oc] looks like when the per-channel zero
points sit near 128, which is what an asymmetric uint8 quantiser gives, and
correlating with nothing is the point: it is a zero point, not something derived
from the weights.

This file has only ever read the scalar weight_tensor->zero_point, but
pipe_tensor carries a zero_points array beside scales and rkt_ml.c already tests
it to decide whether a tensor is per-axis quantised. ROCKET_B_PERCH uses
zero_points[oc] when the array is present.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
index d124bad..7291622 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
@@ -712,9 +712,28 @@ rkt_fill_biases(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
              * zero point at 3x3. Something k-dependent is being added to a MAC
              * that should be zero, and B is the only k-dependent term.
              */
+            /*
+             * ROCKET_B_PERCH: B is PER CHANNEL in the vendor, not per layer.
+             *
+             * Decoded from the runtime capture. sv_rgu's B column holds 26
+             * distinct values across 32 channels, ranging -25 to 23 with a mean
+             * of 0.16, and correlates with nothing: not the bias, the weight
+             * sum, A, C or the scale. A small spread centred on zero is exactly
+             * what 0x80 - wt_zp[oc] looks like when the per-channel zero points
+             * sit near 128, which is what an asymmetric uint8 quantiser
+             * produces.
+             *
+             * This file has only ever used the scalar
+             * `weight_tensor->zero_point`, but `pipe_tensor` carries a
+             * `zero_points` array beside `scales`, and rkt_ml.c already tests
+             * it to decide whether a tensor is per-axis quantised. So the
+             * per-channel zero point is available and has never been used here.
+             */
+            const int *wzp = poperation->conv.weight_tensor->zero_points;
+            int zp_oc = (wzp && getenv("ROCKET_B_PERCH")) ? wzp[oc] : (int)wt_zp;
             *B = getenv("ROCKET_B_VALUE")
                     ? (int16_t)strtol(getenv("ROCKET_B_VALUE"), NULL, 0)
-                    : (int16_t)(0x80 - (int)wt_zp);
+                    : (int16_t)(0x80 - zp_oc);
             /*
              * C is a Q14 per-channel scale ratio (=0x4000 for the max-scale channel).
              * If the HW does NOT apply a built-in >>14 after the BS C-multiply, this
-- 
